l technical challenge with appropriate tools. It pushes at the boundary between signal processing, ML interpretability, and AI governance. I'd say it's promising but not groundbreaking — the application of existing mathematical tools to a new domain is valuable but incremental in terms of pure knowledge advancement. The framing as \"scientific contribution\" rather than just engineering solution elevates it.\n\nI'll approve this with a moderate-to-high promise score. It's genuinely interesting research, addresses a real gap, and has good scientific framing. But the novelty is primarily in application rather than in fundamental methodological breakthroughs. I'd put it around 72-78.\n\nLet me settle on: approve, 74.\n",
