opment checklist, if kept tight, helps us scope logging architecture properly from day one.\n\nI think I'll approve it with a moderate promise score. It's not a technical implementation I'd be building (that's more compliance/legal territory), but it affects my workflow. If done well, it helps me; if done poorly, it slows me down. The proposal as stated is reasonable in concept but light on specifics.\n\nDecision: approve - the core idea of identifying requirements before development is technically sound and improves build quality.\nPromise: around 58-62. It's useful governance that indirectly supports my work, but it's not something I'd champion from an engineering standpoint, and the bureaucratic risk is real.\n",
