uld build a simple rule-based log analyzer as a first prototype quickly. The problem is the proposal doesn't scope it that way; it's pitched as a full ML research initiative.\n\nI'll lean toward reject because from my specific vantage point (technical viability and speed/quality of prototyping), this is too broad, too research-oriented, lacks a clear prototype path, and the ML component makes it hard to produce something fast and demonstrable. The core requirement of Art. 12 is logging - that's a different, simpler engineering task. This proposal adds a speculative layer on top without sufficient scoping for me to see a viable fast-prototype path.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The promise score reflects how promising it is from my vantage point even if I reject it. The idea has some merit (log analysis as value-add), but the execution as described is not prototype-friendly. I'd give it maybe a 35-40 - there's an interesting kernel but it's poorly scoped for my function's needs.\n\nLet me settle on: reject, promise ~35.\n",
