        "content": "{\n  \"screenings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"P2577\",\n      \"rationale\": \"A unified logging infrastructure directly and systematically satisfies Article 12(1)'s mandate for automatic event recording 'over the lifetime of the system' across all high-risk AI systems, standardizes capture of the minimum fields in Article 12(3) (timestamps, reference database, matched input data, verifier identity), and creates a single auditable surface that demonstrates to regulators an organization-level commitment to traceability under Recital 71. From my vantage point, this is precisely the kind of structural safeguard that protects institutional survival: it eliminates the worst regulatory risk in this domain—a patchwork where one project's oversight means non-compliance—and gives us a coherent, defensible narrative for post-market monitoring (Art. 72) and operational oversight (Art. 26(5)).\",\n      \"decision\": \"approve\",\n      \"promise\": 90\n    }\n  ]\n}",
