rts - is sound and directly serves my function's needs. It's not the whole solution but it's a necessary piece. As a Compliance Officer, having this tool means when a market surveillance authority requests information under Article 26(5) or during an audit, I can respond within hours rather than weeks of manual log parsing. That protects institutional survival and reputation.\n\nI'd approve this but with moderate promise score because:\n- It's clearly useful and directly maps to compliance needs (Recital 71 comprehensibility requirement)\n- But it's a layer on top, not the foundation - it doesn't create the logs\n- It lacks several critical compliance dimensions as stated (retention, integrity, specific Annex III fields)\n- The technology choice is vague (\"ELK or similar\") which would need more specification for a compliance commitment\n\nI'd say approve with a promise around 62-68. It's genuinely useful but incomplete and dependent on other infrastructure. Let me settle on 65.\n",
