ided rework\n\n**Resource allocation assessment:**\nThis is a classic \"small upfront cost, large tail risk mitigation\" play. The build cost is modest (a validation script against a known checklist). The downside it prevents (late-stage discovery of logging gaps requiring system redesign) is potentially very expensive and delays market entry. From an efficiency standpoint, this is one of the better risk-adjusted investments you can make in compliance tooling. It's proportional to the regulatory requirement - not over-engineered, not under-scoped.\n\nThe only slight concern: \"checklist of Article 12 requirements\" needs to be maintained as interpretations evolve, but that's a minor ongoing cost. The proposal is appropriately scoped and doesn't commit resources to speculative R&D. It uses existing infrastructure (logs that must exist anyway) and adds a thin validation layer.\n\nI would approve this. From my vantage point of resource efficiency and preventing expensive late-stage surprises, this is a clear win. Promise score: I'd put it around 78-82. It's clearly worth doing, well-scoped, and efficient. Not a 90+ because the \"lightweight\" claim needs to actually hold (if it balloons in scope), and the value depends on the system actually being high-risk under Annex III point 1(a). But as stated, it's a strong efficiency play.\n\nLet me settle on: approve, promise 80.\n",
