iently use resources? \n\nPro:\n- Dual purpose (compliance + science) means you're not paying twice\n- Cultural reframing reduces friction in adoption\n- If the lab already values reproducibility, this is a natural extension\n- The \"automatic recording\" aspect aligns with what good engineering practice demands anyway\n\nCon:\n- \"Research initiative\" = open-ended scope, hard to resource-plan\n- \"Standardized\" schemas could mean building new things vs. adopting existing standards (OpenTelemetry, MLflow schemas, etc.)\n- \"Comprehensive metadata layer... during training AND inference\" is very broad\n- No mention of phasing or leveraging what exists\n\nI'll approve at 65. It's a sound strategic direction that aligns with efficient resource use IF executed with scope discipline, but as written it's ambitious and open-ended in a way that makes resource commitment risky without further scoping.\n",
