ents\" part is the hard part since those aren't generated by code. But if we scope it to automate what CAN be automated (version links, data provenance, training parameters, validation metrics) and leave human-authored sections in a structured format that's at least version-controlled alongside, this is a reasonable investment.\n\nI'll approve with a promise around 62-68. It's operationally sound, leverages existing infrastructure, and reduces recurring burden. The main concern is scope management and the inherent limits of automating narrative risk documentation.\n",
