ents per 12(3)) is a different workstream. This proposal presupposes that's done or being done in parallel.\n\nI think this clears my bar. It supports compliance, enhances our regulatory posture, and leverages the mandatory infrastructure productively. The \"scientific discovery\" framing is slightly off for a compliance function (our job isn't discovery, it's ensuring conformity), but the practical outcome — earlier detection of non-compliance-relevant events — directly serves my mandate.\n\nI'll approve with a moderate-to-high promise score. It's useful and aligned, but it's not the core compliance work itself; it's an enhancement that presupposes the baseline is in place. I'd say around 68-72 range. Let me settle on 70 — it's genuinely valuable for my function (proactive risk detection supports post-market monitoring obligations), but it's secondary to ensuring the logging infrastructure itself meets Article 12's technical requirements, and the research framing means it may not have clear compliance deliverables/timelines.\n",
